            <ArticleTitle>Reversible acute renal failure in association with bilateral ureteral obstruction and hydronephrosis in pregnancy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>239-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This is a case report of a 16-year-old girl with renal failure in pregnancy in association with bilateral ureteral obstruction and hydronephrosis. The presenting symptom was a common nonspecific type of abdominal pain. The diagnosis was made on incidental laboratory work to rule out preeclampsia. Renal function reverted back to normal after induced vaginal delivery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
